\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 ICP \'97 CXO Hive\
We talk to mid-senior operators in India who already do the work. The title and the rooms have not caught up. We do not sell skills training. We sell positioning, visibility, sponsorship, and the jump to the next executive seat.\
Who they are\
India-based. Employed. Large MNC or Indian IT major, typically 1000+ employees (Accenture, Wipro, Infosys, TCS, HCL, Cognizant, Capgemini, plus product / GCC seats at firms like Google, Barclays, Shell, JP Morgan, Citi).\
Senior Manager and above. Typical titles: Senior Manager, Group Manager, Associate Director, Director, Senior Director, VP, SVP, AVP, Head, Principal, General Manager. Experience: 12\'9625 years. Sweet spot: 15\'9620.\
Function: Engineering, Software, Technology, Product, Data, Analytics, AI / ML, Risk, Security, Cybersecurity, Platform, DevOps, Cloud, Infrastructure, QA, IT, Programme.\
Two groups both buy:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Manager / Lead / Architect (~45% of past customers): Senior Manager, Technical Architect, Program Manager, DevSecOps Lead\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Director / VP (~50%): Director, Senior Director, VP, SVP, AVP, Head, Principal, Associate Director\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Primary pool: IT / tech services. Then BFSI, pharma / manufacturing. Cities: Bengaluru, then Mumbai, Gurugram, Pune, Hyderabad.\
They are employed operators inside a real org. Not founders. Not current C-suite. Not jobless.\
What they want\
Seen as the next leader, not the person who runs the machine. A path to CXO / C-suite and a 1Cr+ seat. Promotion that actually happens, not another year of delivery.\
Top pain points\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The work is senior. The title is not.\'a0They have been in the seat long enough that the job is real. The designation and the rooms have not moved with it.\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Hard work already got them here. It will not get them the next one.\'a0Mid-senior was earned by delivery. After that, delivery is assumed. The next jump is positioning, not more output.\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 They have become infrastructure.\'a0People who make the organisation run become invisible until something breaks. Promotion rooms do not reject that profile. They just do not see it.\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	4	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Technical / operating depth, door still closed.\'a0Especially engineering, architect, DevOps, platform, tech leads. The work is there. The right people are not seeing it.\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	5	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Clearest view of the business, still outside the decision room.\'a0Especially product, program, data, analytics, risk, security. They execute strategy. They do not sit where it is set.\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	6	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Results are fine. The CXO conversation never starts.\'a0Especially gen mgmt / ops. Teams, targets, P&L-adjacent work. Nobody has opened the executive path.\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	7	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 GCC / global-room version of the same pain.\'a0They deliver every quarter from India. The promotion goes to whoever is legible in the global room: someone who can be explained in one sentence to people who do not sit next to the work.\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	8	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 No sponsor.\'a0Nobody one or two levels up is carrying their case when they are not in the room. Those calls happen months before the announcement.\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	9	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 No promotion evidence.\'a0The committee needs a paper trail: the problem they own, the number, the risk if they leave. Their CV is a list of delivery. It is not a brief.\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	10	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Presence when they finally get in.\'a0Even with a seat at the table, they do not land as the future leader. Politics, how they relate upward, how they hold the room.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 The four things underneath all of this:\'a0positioning\'a0(known for the problems leadership actually cares about),\'a0sponsorship\'a0(someone in the room making their case),\'a0presence\'a0(how they land),\'a0evidence\'a0(a paper trail a committee can say yes to).\
Not our person (only when it is clear)\
Founders, current C-suite, country heads. Sales, marketing, HR, talent, L&D, design / UX. Coaches, consultants, freelancers. Jobless / not employed. Education, hospitality, staffing, recruiting. Physical supply chain (sourcing, warehousing, SKU availability). Under ~10 years. Outside India. Tiny companies.\
If it is mixed or unclear, they are still our person. Better to include someone off than to drop someone who belongs.\
